      <div type="clause" n="Grið Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> Grið Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Grið Inscr." corresp="#wit-g-b">Be griðe 7 be munde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b">Be griðe 7 be munde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b">Concerning Sanctuary and Protection</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Von Sonderfrieden und von Schutzgewalt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of special peace and of protective authority.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">MS G (Cotton Nero A I, f. 92v, after V Atr., in the same hand c. 1070); the heading is decorated in red. Liebermann dates Grið 1028–1070 and thinks the author was perhaps a Kentishman. K is the same manuscript as the modern edition.</note>
      </div>
